                                Test320
                                -------

  Test for the analysis category:
  - for testing object cycles and objects deleting
  Responsible: Ivana Hrivnacova, IPN Orsay

  This test uses the scenario as defined in test32 based on the basic/B4 example
  with added use-cases for testing analysis

  Run command:
  ./test320  -m run-xyz.mac [-merge on|off] [-vl value]

  Macros:
  run.mac
    - test macro with parameterised output type
  run-xyz.mac, xyz = csv, hdf5, root, xml
    - set the default output type 'xyz' and call run.mac
  run-root-merge.mac
    - as run-root.mac with added appendName alias
      to produce files with different names than
      test without merging activated

  Deleting of objects
  - The objects are deleted after the Run #0 and some of objects
    are re-created after the Run #1

  Output files:
  e-.xyz:
  - contains data collected during 3 e- runs:
    - objects that were not deleted (all with id #0) have three cycles in the file
      (Eg. Edep-0, PX-PY-0, etc.)
    - objects that were deleted and recreated with new name have 1 cycle each
      (eg. Edep-1, Edep-1-new, etc.)
    - ntuple #3 for run #2 (TrackL-3-new)

  e-extra.xyz
  - this file is set before e- run starts to h1 #3 and ntuples #3 and #5
  - contains data collected during 3 runs:
    - h1 #3 for runs #0 and #2 (Edep-3, Edep-3-new)
    - ntuple #3 for run #0 (TrackL-3)
        after deleting without keepSetting, the new ntuple (TrackL-3-new) is in run #2
        written in the default file
    - ntuple #5 for run #0 and #2 (TrackL-5, TrackL-5-new)

  proton.xyz:
  - contains data collected during 2 proton runs (except object written
    in proton-extra.xyz);
    all objects have 2 cycles in the file

  proton-extra.xyz:
  - this file is set before proton run starts to h1 #3 and ntuples #3 and #5;
    all these object have 2 cycles in the file
